This directory contains information about the Mini Board 2.0, a
6811-based robotic controller board.

These subdirectories contain the following:

miniboard/docs/		Manual for the Mini Board controller.  Must
			be printed on a PostScript printer.

miniboard/mac/		Macintosh compiled applications and source
			code for the DLM downloader and Motorola's
			AS11 assembler.

miniboard/ms-dos/	MS-DOS binary and C source code for code
			downloader.  Used to download assembled
			6811 code to the Mini Board.  Motorola's AS11
			assembler for DOS.

miniboard/unix/		source code for downloader, ready to compile
			on Unix machine.

miniboard/lib11/	C and assembler libraries to allow use of
			Dave Dunfield's Micro-C system with the
			Mini Board.  More information in the docs.

miniboard/hexmon/	Program to allow interaction with Mini Board
			hardware (e.g., motor control and sensor
			input) over standard serial line.

miniboard/layout/	Macintosh file (archived using StuffIt and
			BinHex) creating using PCB layout program
			"Professional Layout"; Gerber-format copies
			of the board as well.

miniboard/rb-archive/	Archive of "robot-board" mailing list.
			Lots of Q & A about the Mini Board.

Make sure that you transfer MS-DOS executables using the FTP binary
mode.

For more info, contact Fred Martin (fredm@media.mit.edu).
